<div class="<%= layout_framework_classes %>">
  <div class="<%= layout_framework_title_classes %>">
    <%= render 'framework/page_header', page_name: :content_limiter %>
  </div>

  <div class="<%= layout_framework_content_classes %>">
    <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
      The Content Limiter system automatically restricts the height of content areas based on the view type, ensuring consistent layouts.
      When content exceeds the height threshold, it adds a class that makes text smaller, but content might still overflow.
      It should be used together with the Content component for proper formatting.
    </p>

    <div class="space-y-16">
      <section class="space-y-8">
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <%= framework_heading(3, 'Basic Usage') %>
          <p class="<%= framework_section_description_classes %>">
            To enable automatic content limiting, add the <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">data-content-limiter="true"</code>
            attribute to your content element.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div class="<%= framework_example_classes %>">
            <div class="<%= framework_example_inner_classes %>">
              <div class="<%= framework_example_wrapper_classes %>">
                <div class="screen">
                <div class="view view--full">
                  <div class="layout">
                    <div class="columns">
                      <div class="column">
                        <div class="markdown gap--large">
                          <span class="title">Long Content Example</span>
