                        </div>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                  <div class="title_bar">
                    <%= image_tag plugin_image_path("trmnl--render.svg"), class: "image", alt: "TRMNL Logo" %>
                    <span class="title">Content Limiter</span>
                    <span class="instance">Text Exceeding Threshold</span>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          </div>

          <div class="<%= framework_example_classes %> mt-6">
            <div class="<%= framework_example_inner_classes %>">
              <div class="<%= framework_example_wrapper_classes %>">
                <div class="screen">
                <div class="view view--full">
                  <div class="layout">
                    <div class="columns">
                      <div class="column">
                        <div class="markdown gap--large">
                          <span class="title">Short Content Example</span>
                          <div class="content" data-content-limiter="true">
                            <p>
                              Contrary to what one might think, the Lorem ipsum text, despite being meaningless, has noble origins.
                              <br>
                              <br>
                              Objectively composed of unrelated words, Lorem ipsum owes its existence to Marco Tullio Cicerone and to some steps of his De finibus bonorum et malorum (The highest good and the highest evil) written in 45 BC, a classic of Latin literature dating back more than 2000 years ago.
                              <br>
                              <br>
                              The discovery was made by Richard McClintock , a professor of Latin at Hampden-Sydney College in Virginia, who faced the impetuous recurrence of the dark word consectetur in the text Lorem ipsum researched its origins to identify them in sections 1.10.32 and 1.10.33 of the aforementioned Cicero's philosophical work.
                            </p>
                          </div>
                        </div>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                  <div class="title_bar">
                    <%= image_tag plugin_image_path("trmnl--render.svg"), class: "image", alt: "TRMNL Logo" %>
                    <span class="title">Content Limiter</span>
                    <span class="instance">Text Within Threshold</span>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-4">
            <%= render CodeExampleComponent.new(
              demo_code: '<div class="content" data-content-limiter="true">
  <p>Contrary to what one might think, the Lorem ipsum text, despite being meaningless, has noble...</p>
</div>'
            ) %>
          </div>

          <div class="space-y-4">
            <p class="<%= framework_section_description_classes %>">
              When content exceeds the height threshold (which varies by view type), it will add the <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">content--small</code> class to make text smaller.
              Note that this does not automatically truncate overflowing text. For text truncation with ellipsis, use the <%= link_to 'Clamp', framework_page_path(:clamp, version: '1.2'), class: 'underline' %> component.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-8">
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <%= framework_heading(3, 'Custom Height Threshold') %>
          <p class="<%= framework_section_description_classes %>">
            You can specify a custom maximum height using the <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">data-content-max-height</code> attribute.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div class="<%= framework_example_classes %>">
            <div class="<%= framework_example_inner_classes %>">
              <div class="<%= framework_example_wrapper_classes %>">
                <div class="screen">
                <div class="view view--full">
                  <div class="layout">
                    <div class="columns">
                      <div class="column gap--xxlarge">
                        <div class="markdown gap--large">
                          <span class="title">Custom Height Example</span>
                          <div class="content" data-content-limiter="true" data-content-max-height="140">
                            <p>
                              Contrary to what one might think, the Lorem ipsum text, despite being meaningless, has noble origins.
                              <br>
                              <br>
                              Objectively composed of unrelated words, Lorem ipsum owes its existence to Marco Tullio Cicerone and to some steps of his De finibus bonorum et malorum (The highest good and the highest evil) written in 45 BC, a classic of Latin literature dating back more than 2000 years ago.
